 coatomer with the p24 family of putative cargo receptors. <source>Science.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>1396</fpage>&#x02013;1399.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8703076</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Goldberg, J. <year>1999</year>. Structural and functional analysis of the ARF1-ARFGAP complex reveals a role for coatomer in GTP hydrolysis. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>893</fpage>&#x02013;902.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10102276</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Goldberg, J. <year>2000</year>. Decoding of sorting signals by coatomer through a GTPase switch in the COPI coat complex. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage>671</fpage>&#x02013;679.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10761932</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Gommel, D.U., A.R. Memon, A. Heiss, F. Lottspeich, J. Pfannstiel, J. Lechner, C. Reinhard, J.B. Helms, W. Nickel, and F.T. Wieland. <year>2001</year>. Recruitment to Golgi membranes of ADP-ribosylation factor 1 is mediated by the cytoplasmic domain of p23. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>20</volume>:<fpage>6751</fpage>&#x02013;6760.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11726511</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Helms, J.B., D.J. Palmer, and J.E. Rothman. <year>1993</year>. Two distinct populations of ARF bound to Golgi membranes. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>121</volume>:<fpage>751</fpage>&#x02013;760.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8491770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Huber, I., E. Cukierman, M. Rotman, T. Aoe, V.W. Hsu, and D. Cassel. <year>1998</year>. Requirement for both the amino-terminal catalytic domain and a non-catalytic domain for in vivo activity of ARF1 GAP. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>24786</fpage>&#x02013;24791.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9733781</pub-id></citation></ref><re